zar y normalizados).\n","- `parametros_normalizacion.json`: la mediana, media y desviación de cada medida."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"id":"432b8d53","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:55:15.169779Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:55:15.16945Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.7726Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.771597Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.61089,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.774521+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:15.163631+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Guardados en /kaggle/working/datos : ['entrenamiento.csv', 'entrenamiento_normalizado.csv', 'prueba.csv', 'prueba_normalizado.csv', 'validacion.csv', 'validacion_normalizado.csv', 'parametros_normalizacion.json']\n"]}],"source":["for c in orden:\n","    tabla[tabla.conjunto == c].to_csv(SALIDA / f\"{c}.csv\", index=False)\n","    normalizada[normalizada.conjunto == c].to_csv(SALIDA / f\"{c}_normalizado.csv\", index=False)\n","parametros = {m: {\"mediana\": float(medianas[m]), \"media\": float(medias[m]), \"desviacion\": float(desviaciones[m])}\n","              for m in MEDIDAS}\n","(SALIDA / \"parametros_normalizacion.json\").write_text(json.dumps(parametros, indent=2))\n","print(\"Guardados en\", SALIDA, \":\", sorted(p.name for p in SALIDA.glob(\"*.csv\")) + [\"parametros_normalizacion.json\"])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"09e31717","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004409,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.783809+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.7794+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","## 7. ¿De verdad importa? prueba rápida de la fuga\n","\n","Comparé dos formas de dividir MIT-BIH AF y medí el F1 de la FA con un kNN sencillo:\n","\n","- **Con fuga:** las ventanas se reparten al azar, así que el mismo paciente queda en entrenamiento y en prueba.\n","- **Sin fuga:** se reparten pacientes completos (la división de este notebook). Se evalúa en **validación**, para no tocar la prueba.\n","\n","Si \"con fuga\" sale bastante mejor, es la prueba de que esos números son **inflados**."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":11,"id":"83c1c678","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.794547Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.794177Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.738545Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.737642Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.952008,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.740274+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:16.788266+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>F1 de FA</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>CON fuga (ventanas al azar)</th>\n","      <td>0.963</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>SIN fuga (pacientes separados)</th>\n","      <td>0.986</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                                F1 de FA\n","CON fuga (ventanas al azar)        0.963\n","SIN fuga (pacientes separados)     0.986"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["def f1_fa(entrena_df, evalua_df, k=15):\n","    # Rellena y normaliza con SU propio entrenamiento, entrena kNN y mide el F1 de la FA\n","    med = entrena_df[MEDIDAS].median()\n","    Xe = entrena_df[MEDIDAS].fillna(med); mu, sd = Xe.mean(), Xe.std(ddof=0).replace(0, 1)\n","    Xv = (evalua_df[MEDIDAS].fillna(med) - mu) / sd\n","    knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=min(k, len(Xe))).fit((Xe - mu) / sd, entrena_df.etiqueta)\n","    return f1_score(evalua_df.etiqueta == \"A\", knn.predict(Xv) == \"A\")\n","\n","afdb = tabla[tabla.base == \"MIT-BIH AF\"]\n","ent_mal, eva_mal = train_test_split(afdb, test_size=0.3, random_state=SEMILLA, stratify=afdb.etiqueta)\n","resultados = pd.DataFrame({\n","    \"F1 de FA\": [f1_fa(ent_mal, eva_mal),\n","                 f1_fa(afdb[afdb.conjunto == \"entrenamiento\"], afdb[afdb.conjunto == \"validacion\"])]},\n","    index=[\"CON fuga (ventanas al azar)\", \"SIN fuga (pacientes separados)\"]).round(3)\n","display(resultados)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"fa9d5dce","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.750674Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.75031Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.756519Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.755413Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.013532,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.758221+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.744689+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["__notebook__.ipynb: 115.05 KB (0.11 MB)\n"]}],"source":["import os\n","\n","# Ver todos los archivos generados en la carpeta de trabajo y su peso\n","for archivo in os.listdir('/kaggle/working'):\n","    ruta = os.path.join('/kaggle/working', archivo)\n","    if os.path.isfile(ruta):\n","        peso_kb = os.path.getsize(ruta) / 1024\n","        print(f\"{archivo}: {peso_kb:.2f} KB ({peso_kb/1024:.2f} MB)\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"id":"19c74de6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.768704Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.768321Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-25T21:55:18.00745Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-25T21:55:18.006277Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.246612,"end_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:18.009374+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-25T21:55:17.762762+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[